{
 "title": "Enums and match",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "An **`enum`** lists the options (**variants**) a value can take. To look at an enum value you use **`match`**. Its most important feature: the compiler checks that **all cases** are handled. If you forget a variant, the code does not compile."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "enum TrafficLight:",
    "    Red",
    "    Yellow",
    "    Green",
    "",
    "fn action(light: TrafficLight):",
    "    match light:",
    "        TrafficLight.Red:",
    "            print(\"Stop!\")",
    "        TrafficLight.Yellow:",
    "            print(\"Get ready...\")",
    "        TrafficLight.Green:",
    "            print(\"Go!\")",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    action(TrafficLight.Red)",
    "    action(TrafficLight.Green)"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "Stop!",
    "Go!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "If you do not want to write them all out, `_:` catches everything else."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "enum TrafficLight:",
    "    Red",
    "    Yellow",
    "    Green",
    "",
    "fn is_stop(light: TrafficLight) -> bool:",
    "    match light:",
    "        TrafficLight.Red:",
    "            return true",
    "        _:",
    "            return false",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    print(is_stop(TrafficLight.Red), is_stop(TrafficLight.Yellow))"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "true false"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "exercise",
   "id": "c06-l01-x1",
   "prompt": "For the enum `Direction` (`North`, `South`, `East`, `West`), write `name(d)`: it prints its own name (`north`, `south`...). Call it for `West`.",
   "starter": [
    "enum Direction:",
    "    North",
    "    South",
    "    East",
    "    West",
    "",
    "fn name(d: Direction):",
    "    match d:",
    "        Direction.North:",
    "            print(\"north\")",
    "        _:",
    "            print(\"?\")",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    name(Direction.West)"
   ],
   "solution": [
    "enum Direction:",
    "    North",
    "    South",
    "    East",
    "    West",
    "",
    "fn name(d: Direction):",
    "    match d:",
    "        Direction.North:",
    "            print(\"north\")",
    "        Direction.South:",
    "            print(\"south\")",
    "        Direction.East:",
    "            print(\"east\")",
    "        Direction.West:",
    "            print(\"west\")",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    name(Direction.West)"
   ],
   "hint": "Write one branch for each variant; leave out the `_`.",
   "expected": [
    "west"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "quiz",
   "id": "c06-l01-q1",
   "q": "What happens if you forget a variant inside `match`?",
   "options": [
    "It crashes at run time",
    "The code does not compile",
    "It is skipped silently"
   ],
   "answer": 1,
   "why": "`match` is exhaustive: a missing case is a compile error."
  }
 ]
}
